-- title:
--   Weighted homogeneous components of a product with a homogeneous factor
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $\sigma$ a set of variables, $G$ an additive abelian group and $w:\sigma\to G$ a weight function. The weight of a monomial $x^m$ (with $m\in\mathbb{N}^{(\sigma)}$ finitely supported) is $\mathrm{wt}(m)=\sum_s m_s\,w(s)\in G$. For $p\in K[x_\sigma]$ and $d\in G$ let $[p]_d$ denote the weighted homogeneous component of $p$ of weight $d$, the sum of the terms of $p$ whose monomials have weight $d$. A polynomial $a$ is weighted homogeneous of weight $e$ if every monomial occurring in $a$ has weight $e$ (the zero polynomial is homogeneous of every weight).
--
--   If $a$ is weighted homogeneous of weight $e\in G$, then for every polynomial $g\in K[x_\sigma]$ and every $d\in G$,
--   $$[a\,g]_d=a\,[g]_{d-e}.$$
--
--   Multiplication by a homogeneous element shifts the grading by its weight, so extracting a component commutes with it up to this shift. The identity is the basic tool for showing that ideals generated by weighted homogeneous polynomials are homogeneous, and for describing the graded pieces of such ideals.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $[p]_d$ is `weightedHomogeneousComponent w d p` and homogeneity is `IsWeightedHomogeneous w a e`; no finiteness of $\sigma$ is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/Determinantal/Multigraded.lean#L20-L44

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SmoothInitialForm
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_Multigraded

open OAI OAI.PermanentBorder OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded
open MvPolynomial
variable {K σ G : Type*} [Field K] [AddCommGroup G]
variable (w : σ → G)

theorem OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded.project_mul {a : MvPolynomial σ K} {e : G}
    (ha : a.IsWeightedHomogeneous w e) (g : MvPolynomial σ K) (d : G) :
    weightedHomogeneousComponent w d (a * g) =
      a * weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d-e) g := by sorry
